+WebAssembly Micro Runtime (WAMR) is a lightweight, configurable WebAssembly runtime for embedded, IoT, edge, cloud, and trusted-execution environments. Its main components include:
+
+* [**VMcore**](./core/iwasm/): Runtime libraries for loading and executing WebAssembly modules through interpretation, ahead-of-time compilation, or just-in-time compilation.
+* [**iwasm**](./product-mini/): A command-line runtime built with WAMR VMcore and WASI support.
+* [**wamrc**](./wamr-compiler/): The WAMR ahead-of-time compiler.
+* Supporting projects: [App Framework](https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wamr-app-framework/blob/main/app-framework/README.md), [App Manager](https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wamr-app-framework/blob/main/app-mgr/README.md), [WAMR IDE](./test-tools/wamr-ide)
+
+## Migration Membrane Prototype
+
+This repository extends WAMR with the runtime prototype accompanying our work on the **Virtual Stationarity Runtime (VSR)**. VSR treats recurrent migration between passing satellite hosts as a steady-state execution primitive rather than an exceptional infrastructure operation.
+
+The prototype implements the runtime-side handover mechanisms described in the paper. It does **not** implement orbital prediction, successor selection, migration scheduling, or network path control. These responsibilities belong to an external orbital orchestrator, which supplies the successor host, trigger time, and migration budget.
+
