+## Paper-to-Code Mapping
+
+| Paper concept                         | Purpose                                                                                     | Primary implementation                                                                                                                          |
+| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| Portable Execution (X)         | Represents execution independently of the source OS and ISA                                 | Upstream WAMR classic interpreter                                                                                                               |
+| State Capture and Restoration (S) | Captures a relocatable base state and restores it on the successor                          | [`wasm_live_migration.c`](./core/iwasm/common/wasm_live_migration.c), [`wasm_interp_classic.c`](./core/iwasm/interpreter/wasm_interp_classic.c) |
+| Continuous State Projection (P) | Records host-interaction outcomes and memory mutations while the source continues executing | [`wasm_live_migration.c`](./core/iwasm/common/wasm_live_migration.c)                                                                            |
+| Capability Virtualization (V)  | Rebinds logical capabilities to target-local resources                                      | [`libc_wasi_wrapper.c`](./core/iwasm/libraries/libc-wasi/libc_wasi_wrapper.c), [`wasm_wasi_proxy.c`](./core/iwasm/common/wasm_wasi_proxy.c), [`wasm_live_migration.c`](./core/iwasm/common/wasm_live_migration.c)   |
